<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14465" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">distĭchus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίστιχος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>consisting of two rows.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hordeum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 9, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> ‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">distĭ-chum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>a building with two
				stories</i> or <i>two rows of chambers</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. p. 627</span></i>, <i>no.</i> 234.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">distĭchon</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>a poem of two
				verses</i>, <i>a distich</i> consisting of a
			hexameter and a pentameter, <i><span class="en">Mart. 8,
				29, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Oth. 3 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
